      en: "The ruins of the royal palace of Kavumu in Gitega Province date from the 19th century and were a residence of Burundian kings. The palace consisted of several grass and wood huts on a hill. After the death of King Mwezi IV Gisabo in 1908, the compound fell into disrepair. Today only foundations and some wall remnants remain. The site is a national cultural heritage and is revered as sacred by locals. Regular traditional ceremonies are held.",
