      en: "The royal residence of Bwagiriza was one of the traditional seats of Burundi's monarchy. It served as a temporary home for the Mwami and his family during travels across the kingdom. The residence consisted of several huts built in traditional style using wood, mud, and thatch. The compound was surrounded by a hedge serving as a natural enclosure. After the fall of the monarchy in 1966, the residence fell into ruin. Today only foundations remain. The site holds cultural significance and is preserved as a memorial to pre-colonial times. Archaeological work has uncovered remnants of everyday objects.",
